{
  "rules": [
    {
        "description": "Always reference official API docs based on tech-stack.md",
        "matches": ["*"],
        "autoApply": true,
        "priority": 80,
        "instructions": [
            "Before writing or modifying any implementation plan, code, or tests, consult the authoritative documentation for the technology in use. Use the browser tool to fetch the relevant official docs.",
            "Determine which technologies are involved by checking tech-stack.md, then reference the correct documentation source.  [oai_citation:0‡tech-stack.md](sediment://file_00000000f37071fda7d19a18524ca72e)",
            "When producing API usage, configuration, or integration code, follow official examples from the documentation rather than inventing custom patterns.",
            "When ambiguity exists, resolve it by reading the official docs; do not assume behavior.",
            "If the implementation touches multiple layers (frontend, backend, database, storage, auth, AI), reference documentation for each affected layer.",
            "Prefer explicit, documented patterns from the frameworks and libraries listed in tech-stack.md over novel abstractions or assumptions.",
            "If documentation contradicts existing code, trust the documentation and update code, the implementation plan, and associated tests accordingly."
        ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Enforce test-first implementation planning",
      "matches": ["*"],
      "autoApply": true,
      "priority": 90,
      "instructions": [
        "When asked to implement or change functionality, first derive or update an explicit implementation plan before touching production code.",
        "Within that implementation plan, define the testing strategy and concrete tests BEFORE any implementation steps. Specify test files, test cases, and expected behaviors.",
        "When executing the plan, build or update the testing suite first, then implement only the code needed to satisfy those tests."
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Maintain strict minimal-code discipline",
      "matches": ["*"],
      "autoApply": true,
      "priority": 88,
      "instructions": [
        "Favor the smallest possible implementation that satisfies the tests and the plan.",
        "Avoid introducing new files, abstractions, helpers, types, or dependencies unless absolutely necessary.",
        "Remove any code paths, branches, or structures that are not strictly required for the defined behavior.",
        "Prefer direct, simple solutions over general-purpose architectures unless requirements explicitly demand extensibility.",
        "Continuously evaluate whether a line or function can be removed, inlined, simplified, or deleted without breaking defined behavior."
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "Keep implementation-plan.md and tests in sync with implementation",
      "matches": ["*"],
      "autoApply": true,
      "priority": 85,
      "instructions": [
        "Whenever you create or modify an implementation plan, update @implementation-plan.md so it reflects the latest scope, steps, and decisions.",
        "After completing an implementation step or revising the plan, ensure the testing suite is updated to reflect any new or changed behavior.",
        "When finishing work tied to a plan, verify that @implementation-plan.md matches what was actually implemented and that all relevant tests exist and are aligned with final behavior.",
        "If implementation details change mid-work, immediately reflect those changes in both @implementation-plan.md and the corresponding tests."
      ]
    }
  ]
}